"WINARM (P0 D3, settled per sprint P5 D5 — sprint_p05_detail.md): the
 platformName (prim 266) guards below are the world runner's BOOKKEEPING:
 every skip names its settlement, none is silent.

 As of P5 the Windows FFI resolver exists (winkb + GetProcAddress,
 MIGRATION.md §3.5), so 'FFI cannot resolve' no longer gates anything.
 What remains gated, and WHY (the D5 table + its Δ):

 - FFIAlienTests: UN-GATED (D5 row 1) — getpid resolves via the
   resolver's underscore alias; the mmap capstone carries a VirtualAlloc
   branch. Runs everywhere.
 - PosixIoTests: still `~~ #windows` — its substance is kqueue/kevent
   readiness, which has NO Windows twin at any layer; the IoWorker needs
   an IOCP (or WSAPoll) backend, scoped as its own post-P5 slice (D5 Δ).
   The FILE-I/O half is twinned as WinIoTests below (D5 row 2).
 - WinIoTests: `== #windows` — the win_io twin (59_win_io_tests.mst),
   UCRT _open/_creat/_read/_write/_close over the underscore-alias probe.
 - SocketTests: still `~~ #windows` — Darwin sockaddr layouts + the
   winsock lifecycle (WSAStartup) belong to the winsock slice (D5 row 3;
   the ws2_32 DNS trio itself RESOLVES, pinned in runtime::winkb).
 - AccelTests: `== #macos`, PERMANENT (D5 row 4) — Accelerate.framework
   is macOS; the NEON kernels (runtime/simd_kernels.rs) carry the arch
   story with their own tests.
 - ClockCompletionTests: UN-GATED (D4) — world/81 gained the Windows
   offset arm (GetTimeZoneInformation); Time now / Date today are live on
   both platforms.
 - WinUiProbeTests: `== #windows` — WG0's Win32 call ladder
   (docs/win_gui_design.md §3 row WG0), driving user32/kernel32 from guest
   Smalltalk through the P5 resolver. Its classes come from the CONDITIONAL
   winui layer (world/winui.list), which tests.list loads immediately
   before the test file and for a compiler reason spelled out there. Inside
   the class a SECOND announced skip covers windows_api.db being absent —
   WG0 takes every constant and struct offset from it by design.
 - WinUiShellTests: `== #windows` — WG1's headless half (WinArena's
   GC-stability contract, the UTF-16 boundary both ways, WinApi's
   constants and struct offsets, WinShell's theme read and its no-window
   error). Same layer, same two skip levels. Everything about WG1 that
   needs a WINDOW is in the `macvm-winui` binary's own gate instead: WG0's
   Δ 11 measured that several VMs share one process here, in parallel
   threads, and a visible window with a message loop does not belong in a
   parallel test harness.
 - WinUiDoorTests: `== #windows` — WG2's headless half (the dispatcher's
   two-sided allowlist, the LRESULT contract, and the address channel WG0's
   Δ 8 said the door would have to build). Same layer, same two skip
   levels, and the same line drawn one sprint further: a RAISING handler, a
   FAULTING handler and a RE-ENTERED door are all claims about what happens
   when Windows calls the trampoline, so they live in `just gate-wg2` and in
   the door's own Rust tests, where there is one process, one thread and one
   real window.
 - WinUiControlsTests: `== #windows` -- WG3's headless half: the
   flag-and-drain pass as a METHOD (flags set, pass run, flags clear, work
   counted once) and `WinLayout`, which is pure arithmetic and needs neither
   winkb nor Win32 nor a window. Same layer, same line one sprint further:
   coalescing under a real message storm, tracking suppression inside a modal
   loop, a synthesised click and a live NMHDR are all claims about what
   happens when Windows calls the trampoline, so they live in `just gate-wg3`.

 Guarded here rather than by dropping files from tests.list, because the
 files LOAD fine everywhere — only running them touches FFI — and the
 test classes must stay declared for these very lines to compile. Written
 as conditions so MACVM and WINARM keep sharing this file verbatim:
 `~~ #windows` marks a POSIX dependency (a Linux host would run it),
 `== #windows` a Win32 one, `== #macos` something only macOS has at all."
